# Phase 18 compatibility release gate — 2026-10-23 19:20:26 UTC

Base revision: `875e47d9` on `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`.
Implementation changes are committed independently; this append-only record
refreshes local P18-V02 evidence and records a narrow P18-V01 correction.

## P18-V01 findings

- Pinned RocketMQ 5.5.1 `NettyRemotingClient.java` source SHA-256:
  `b9822a1abb0710070de051e7f94e0ba5facbf3284f3ae09977de14aee952476d`.
  `scanAvailableNameSrv()` submits NameServer probes in configured order to a
  4-core/10-max executor with a 32-entry queue; the default `AbortPolicy`
  rejects and aborts the remainder of the scan pass at saturation.
- Pinned `ThreadUtils.java` source SHA-256:
  `3aef35aa3f9f42eeb8da63e89f0a47b1eecfbe0e13ca2e460cf6be520a48d479`.
  Rust now submits only the configured-order prefix within its 42-slot bound,
  starts later ticks at the first address, and applies completed tasks before
  recalculating capacity. The remoting test pins prefix and restart ordering.
- Unix offset store writer leases now use non-inherited POSIX `fcntl(F_SETLK)`
  record locks with explicit unlock on drop. The lock file remains linked to
  avoid replacement-inode races. A subprocess regression verifies exclusion
  while another process owns a store and acquisition after drop. The focused
  test passed; three consecutive parallel all-feature Consumer library suites
  passed (264 tests each).

