- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D
  warnings` — passed.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` — passed.
- `bash tests/stress/run-offline-smoke.sh` — passed 20 cases × 3.
- `cargo run --offline --locked -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --example
  fuzz_smoke` — passed 163 frame seeds, 11 message seeds, 2,784 bounded
  mutations, 245 frame decodes, and 192 message decodes.
- `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test` and
  `--validate-manifest` — passed; all 37 scenarios validated.
- `mvn -o -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` — passed: 37 scenarios,
  Java 5.5.1 runtime probes, fixture drift checks, 11 message fixtures, 106
  typed headers, 19 typed bodies, and Java/Rust cross-decodes.
- Workspace metadata/license/dependency checks, release example build, and
  offline benchmark passed. Benchmark sample is appended to
  `docs/compatibility/PHASE_18_OFFLINE_BENCHMARK_BASELINE.md`; it sets no
  threshold.
- Windows GNU all-target/all-feature workspace `cargo check` and strict
  Clippy passed as compile-only evidence.
- Workspace Rustdoc JSON generation passed. Inventory counts remain
  name-level evidence, not behavioral proof.

## Remaining scope

This closes the NameServer scan admission/order mismatch and strengthens Unix
offset writer lock release only. Broad P18-V01 source/API/settings/input/error/
control-flow and reverse-export reconciliation remains PARTIAL. Native Windows
runtime, current-revision remote CI, and Phase 19 Broker/Docker scenarios were
not run. No plan was edited, no push or remote CI was run, and the four
pre-existing Phase 19 paths remain untouched and unstaged.
